Program overview:
This program is a console game based on a sonnet
The program prints the sonnet from the beginning
It stops at a random word and hides that word with underscores
Nothing after the missing word is printed
The user is asked to type the missing word
The program tells the user if the answer is correct or incorrect
The game repeats until the user gets three correct answers or three incorrect answers

Input and output:
The input is a word typed by the user
The output is part of the sonnet with one word hidden
The program also prints feedback and the current score

Definition of a word:
A word is any space separated token in the sonnet
Punctuation is considered part of the word
For example dignity, includes the comma
Answers are checked without considering letter case

Program design:
The sonnet is stored as an array of lines
This keeps the original line formatting
The program scans the sonnet and records every word position
Each word position stores the line number and word number

Game flow:
At the start of each round a random word position is chosen
The program makes sure the same word is not chosen twice in a row
All lines before the missing word are printed normally
The line with the missing word is printed only up to that word
The missing word is replaced with underscores
The program then asks the user for the missing word

Ending condition:
The game ends when the user reaches three correct answers
The game also ends if the user reaches three incorrect answers

Tests:
The tests are in a separate file called tests.java
The tests check underscore creation
The tests check word comparison logic
The tests check that output stops at the missing word
The tests check that the random word changes between rounds